# Shared by BOTH Vercel projects. There is exactly one .vercelignore and it
# is read from the repository root, before Root Directory is applied -- so an
# entry here is excluded from the landing build and the reviewer build alike.
#
# That is why `site/` is NOT listed. Excluding it to slim the reviewer's
# bundle also deleted the landing project's package.json out from under its
# own `npm ci`, which failed the build three seconds in. site/ stays; its
# source is a few hundred kB, and node_modules and dist are already excluded
# below. tests/test_site.py pins this so it cannot be "optimised" back.
#
# The other direction of the same trap: everything
# scripts/vercel_reviewer_build.py needs at build time must stay --
# runs/realistic-seed42/ (the committed inputs), .llm_cache/ (so the contract
# compile needs no API key), calibration/ (the audit reads the pinned
# artifact), and datagen/ (imported when `python -m cli` loads the full Typer
# app; never reachable from the served application -- see the import-closure
# note in requirements.txt).

node_modules/
site/dist/
site/*.tsbuildinfo
reviewer/web/dist/
reviewer/web/*.tsbuildinfo

tests/
chaos/
docs/
eval/results/

.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
